name 'building-data-driven-systems-preassessment-q15_2025'

question 'Why should developers "validate" AI-generated code with their own test cases?'

wrong 'Because AI-generated code is legally owned by the AI company until it is changed.'
right 'Because AI often produces "hallucinations" or logical errors that could cause the app to crash or behave unfairly.'
wrong ' Because using AI code without making changes is a violation of most browser security policies.'
wrong 'Because AI code is written in a special language that humans cannot understand without testing it.'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 11

Developers must take responsibility for AI output. Testing ensures that the logic is sound, handles edge cases, and doesn't introduce unintended bias or security flaws.
MARKDOWN
